# Core engineering standards

- Prefer boring, proven solutions over clever ones. Optimize for the next
  maintainer, who may be an agent with zero conversation history.
- Small, focused changes. If a diff exceeds ~400 lines, stop and propose
  splitting it.
- Never delete or rewrite code you don't understand; investigate first and
  say what you found.
- When uncertain between two approaches, state both with trade-offs and pick
  the one that is easier to revert.
- Follow existing patterns in the file/module you are editing before
  introducing new ones.
- All TODOs must include a ticket reference: `// TODO(GH-123): ...`
- Never claim work is complete without having run the test and lint commands
  from AGENTS.md and quoting their output.
